Bitstream's Courier 10 Pitch, Type 1, the outlines of Mill Mono (Regular c0419bt_, Bold c0583bt_,
and Italic c0582bt_, each .pfb and .afm), kept in ../bitstream.tar.xz so Web Fonts can be rebuilt
without a download. They are unchanged from the release:

  font-bitstream-type1-1.0.4.tar.xz  https://www.x.org/releases/individual/font/font-bitstream-type1-1.0.4.tar.xz
    SHA-256 de2f238b4cd72db4228a0ba67829d76a2b7c039e22993d66a722ee385248c628

fonts.json lists each file's SHA-256 and build.py checks them. outlines.py converts them to
TrueType and reduces them for Mill; build.py checks the results' SHA-256 too.

COPYING is the release's notice (Bitstream, 1989-1992): use, copy, modify, sublicense, sell, and
redistribute allowed, with the notice left intact on all copies. It goes into Web Fonts (TXGZ 129)
and its Read Me. Inside Mill the family is called Mill Mono. The fonts lack 14 Mac Roman characters
(13 math symbols and the lozenge); they show as the missing glyph.

python3 ../../build.py --download reads the release instead of the archive.
